614 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 74 0 R/T(A relation is in BCNF when every non-trivial FD determinant is a superkey. The relations above are BCNF under the stated dependencies, provided the address rule is represented carefully. In ADDRESS, AddressID is the key and \(ShipStreet, ShipCity\) is also a candidate key because it determines ShipPIN and AddressID identifies the address. Add UNIQUE\(ShipStreet, ShipCity\). In POSTAL, ShipPIN is the key. All remaining determinants are keys. )/E(A relation is in BCNF when every non-trivial FD determinant is a superkey. The relations above are BCNF under the stated dependencies, provided the address rule is represented carefully. In ADDRESS, AddressID is the key and \(ShipStreet, ShipCity\) is also a candidate key because it determines ShipPIN and AddressID identifies the address. Add UNIQUE\(ShipStreet, ShipCity\). In POSTAL, ShipPIN is the key. All remaining determinants are keys. )/Pg 18 0 R/K[28]>>
endobj

