638 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 75 0 R/T(TheBCNF relation PRODUCT_TAG_COLOUR\(ProductID, Tag, Colour\) may be in BCNF because ProductID does not functionally determine one Tag or Colour. However, it stores every combination. With t tags and c colours it contains t \327 c rows for one product. For 3 tags and 4 colours, it stores 12 rows. )/E(TheBCNF relation PRODUCT_TAG_COLOUR\(ProductID, Tag, Colour\) may be in BCNF because ProductID does not functionally determine one Tag or Colour. However, it stores every combination. With t tags and c colours it contains t \327 c rows for one product. For 3 tags and 4 colours, it stores 12 rows. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

639 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 75 0 R/T(Decompose into PRODUCT_TAG\(ProductID, Tag\) and PRODUCT_COLOUR\(ProductID, Colour\). The same product now needs t + c rows: 3 + 4 = 7 rows, instead of 12. The decomposition removes the non-trivial MVDs from each relation and is in 4NF. Every 4NF )/E(Decompose into PRODUCT_TAG\(ProductID, Tag\) and PRODUCT_COLOUR\(ProductID, Colour\). The same product now needs t + c rows: 3 + 4 = 7 rows, instead of 12. The decomposition removes the non-trivial MVDs from each relation and is in 4NF. Every 4NF )/Pg 19 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

