<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 76 0 R/T(A two-projection decomposition is generally lossy here: for example, projecting on SC and CW can combine a supplier-category pair with a category-warehouse pair without checking that the supplier delivers to that warehouse. The missing SW relationship permits spurious triples. The same issue occurs if any one of the three pairwise projections is omitted. )/E(A two-projection decomposition is generally lossy here: for example, projecting on SC and CW can combine a supplier-category pair with a category-warehouse pair without checking that the supplier delivers to that warehouse. The missing SW relationship permits spurious triples. The same issue occurs if any one of the three pairwise projections is omitted. )/Pg 20 0 R/K[32]>>
