982 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 85 0 R/T(A five-table order-history query repeated 200,000 times per day can create significant join and I/O work. However, normalized joins are not automatically too slow: primary-key/foreign-key indexes, a covering index, caching and a selective customer/order filter can make them efficient. A separate PRICE_HISTORY\(ProductID, ValidFrom, ValidTo, UnitPrice\) relation can reconstruct catalogue price at order time, but adds a date-range join and requires unambiguous effective periods. Storing the actual paid price directly in ORDER_ITEM is simpler and preserves the exact transaction fact. A covering index can further accelerate common history queries. )/E(A five-table order-history query repeated 200,000 times per day can create significant join and I/O work. However, normalized joins are not automatically too slow: primary-key/foreign-key indexes, a covering index, caching and a selective customer/order filter can make them efficient. A separate PRICE_HISTORY\(ProductID, ValidFrom, ValidTo, UnitPrice\) relation can reconstruct catalogue price at order time, but adds a date-range join and requires unambiguous effective periods. Storing the actual paid price directly in ORDER_ITEM is simpler and preserves the exact transaction fact. A covering index can further accelerate common history queries. )/Pg 29 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

